  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn intransitive verb. The subject is the thing that gets interrupted — conversation, signal, stream of people, music, etc. Often used in the te-form {途切|とぎ}れて to describe a resulting state.\n\nFORMS:\n- {途切|とぎ}れ{途切|とぎ}れ: intermittently, in fragments (e.g., {途切|とぎ}れ{途切|とぎ}れに{聞|き}こえる \"to hear in fragments\")\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {会話|かいわ}が{途切|とぎ}れる: conversation breaks off\n- {電波|でんぱ}が{途切|とぎ}れる: signal cuts out\n- {人通|ひとどお}りが{途切|とぎ}れる: foot traffic stops\n- {連絡|れんらく}が{途切|とぎ}れる: contact is lost\n- {集中力|しゅうちゅうりょく}が{途切|とぎ}れる: concentration is broken",
